   "title": "Ballon d’Or: Six journalists rank Messi first",
   "url": "https://punchng.com/ballon-dor-six-journalists-rank-messi-first/",
   "domain": "punchng.com",
   "source": "Punch（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:25:20 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793471120.0,
   "ageDays": 0.0,
   "summary": "Despite finishing fifth in the 2026 men’s Ballon d’Or rankings, Lionel Messi received first-place votes from six countries, including traditional rivals Brazil. Each journalist’s first-place selection earned Messi 15 points, contributing to his final tally of 612 points. Brazil’s decision to rank Messi first was among the notable voting choices, given the country’s long-standing football rivalry with Argentina.",
   "summary_zh": "尽管在2026年男子金球奖评选中仅排名第五，利昂内尔·梅西仍获得了包括传统对手巴西在内的6个国家投出的第一名选票。每位记者投出的第一名为梅西贡献15分，他最终累计获得612分。鉴于巴西与阿根廷在足球领域长期存在的竞争关系，巴西决定将梅西排在首位，成为此次投票中值得关注的投票选择之一。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Despite finishing fifth in the 2026 men’s Ballon d’Or rankings, Lionel Messi received first-place votes from six countries, including traditional rivals Brazil. The voting breakdown released by France Football on its website on Friday showed that journalists representing Argentina, Brazil, Belarus, China, Panama and the United Arab Emirates ranked the Inter Miami forward as the best player in the world. Each journalist’s first-place selection earned Messi 15 points, contributing to his final tally of 612 points. The 39-year-old finished fifth in the overall rankings, behind winner Harry Kane, Kylian Mbappé, Lamine Yamal and Rodri. Brazil’s decision to rank Messi first was among the notable voting choices, given the country’s long-standing football rivalry with Argentina. Ballon d’Or: Nigeria’s voter picked Rodri over Kane Kane beat Mbappé by less than 41 points to win Ballon d’Or — Organisers From Harry Kane to Musiala: Bayern Munich players’ weekly salaries revealed – Report Kane won the award with 1,055 points, just 28 ahead of Mbappé, who finished second with 1,027 points. Yamal came third with 881 points, while Rodri occupied fourth position with 726 points. Messi’s six first-place votes were more than the number received by 2025 winner Ousmane Dembélé, who did not finish first on any of the 100 ballots. Dembélé, who placed seventh overall with 418 points, was ranked second by journalists from Burkina Faso, China, France, Georgia, Haiti, North Macedonia and Nigeria. The 2026 award was the fourth-closest men’s Ballon d’Or vote in the competition’s history, with Kane edging Mbappé by 28 points. Okiki Adeduyite Okiki is a journalist with over seven years experience covering politics, foreign news, society, entertainment and the film industry",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
