   "summary": "The governorship candidate of the Nigeria Democratic Congress (NDC) in Kano State, Aminu Abdussalam Gwarzo, and his running mate, Mustapha Rabiu Kwankwaso, are still missing from the updated final list of candidates released by the Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC). The updated list released on Saturday, retained the omission of the NDC candidates.",
   "summary_zh": "尼日利亚民主党（INEC）在卡诺州竞选州长的 Aminu Abdussalam Gwarzo 及其竞选搭档 Mustapha Rabiu Kwankwaso，仍未出现在独立国家选举委员会（INEC）最新发布的最终候选人名单中。周六发布的更新名单保留了将 NDC 候选人排除在外的做法。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The governorship candidate of the Nigeria Democratic Congress (NDC) in Kano State, Aminu Abdussalam Gwarzo, and his running mate, Mustapha Rabiu Kwankwaso, are still missing from the updated final list of candidates released by the Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC). The updated list released on Saturday, retained the omission of the NDC candidates. Among those listed are Governor Abba Kabir Yusuf and Murtala Sule Garo of the APC, Abacha Muhammad Sani and Kibiya Yusuf Ado of the PDP, and Ibrahim Ali Amin and Shehu Abdulkadir Bari of the ADC. Recall that the NDC had blamed an error for the omission of its candidate and his running mate from the list of candidates published by the Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC) in the initial release. Dr Yusuf Ibrahim Kofarmata, Secretary of the Kwankwasiyya Caucus and the NDC House of Representatives candidate in Kano in a statement, at the time, said the party had received assurances that the omission resulted from an error in entering the candidates’ details. Comments expressed here do not reflect the opinions of Vanguard newspapers or any employee thereof",
