   "title": "BREAKING: Gov. Lawal Presents Staff Of Office To New Emir Of Gusau, 18 Others",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/breaking-gov-lawal-presents-staff-of-office-to-new-emir-of-gusau-18-others/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:13:51 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793463231.0,
   "ageDays": 0.07,
   "summary": "The new Emir of Gusau, a direct descendant of Malam Sambo Dan Ashafa, founder of the Gusau Emirate, was appointed in July 2025 following the death of his father, Alhaji Ibrahim Bello, on July 25, 2025, at age 71. Presenting the Staff of Office, Governor Lawal described the new Emir as a gentle, compassionate and humble personality with the capacity to lead.",
   "summary_zh": "古绍新任埃米尔是古绍埃米尔国创始人马拉姆·桑博·达·阿沙法的直系后裔。他的父亲哈吉·易卜拉欣·贝洛于2025年7月25日去世，享年71岁；古绍新任埃米尔于2025年7月获任命。州长拉瓦尔授予其权杖时，称这位新任埃米尔为人温和、富有同情心且谦逊，具备领导能力。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The colourful coronation ceremony held at the Trade Fair Complex in Gusau was attended by thousands of subjects, traditional title holders, top government officials, and dignitaries from across the North-West. The new Emir of Gusau, a direct descendant of Malam Sambo Dan Ashafa, founder of the Gusau Emirate, was appointed in July 2025 following the death of his father, Alhaji Ibrahim Bello, on July 25, 2025, at age 71. Gusau Emirate, with roots in the 19th-century Sokoto Jihad, remains the cultural and political heart of Zamfara State. Presenting the Staff of Office, Governor Lawal described the new Emir as a gentle, compassionate and humble personality with the capacity to lead. He charged all traditional rulers in the state to join hands with government at all levels to restore lasting peace and stability, noting that insecurity can only be defeated through collective effort. “Traditional leaders are custodians of our people and our cultural heritage. You must serve as beacons of unity, peace and development and promote harmonious coexistence among your subjects and beyond,” Lawal said. He expressed optimism that the reign of the 16th Emir of Gusau would usher in phenomenal socio-economic development for the Emirate, Zamfara State and Nigeria as a whole. Responding, the Emir of Gusau, HRH Alhaji Abdulkadir Ibrahim Bello II, pledged to provide purposeful leadership that will promote peace, security and development. He assured that he would stand by all his subjects, foster unity and attract development to the emirate, while calling on the people to remain law-abiding and supportive of government policies. Pre-coronation activities included a Public Lecture on the history and life of the founder of Gusau, Malam Sambo Dan Ashafa, by renowned scholars, and a grand turbaning ceremony of distinguished personalities who have contributed to the growth of the Emirate and Zamfara State. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
