   "title": "NSCDC suspends officer over Abuja Market shooting, orders trial",
   "url": "https://www.vanguardngr.com/2026/10/nscdc-suspends-officer-over-abuja-market-shooting-orders-trial/",
   "domain": "vanguardngr.com",
   "source": "vanguardngr.com",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:13:48 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793463228.0,
   "ageDays": 0.07,
   "summary": "The Nigeria Security and Civil Defence Corps (NSCDC) has suspended Deputy Superintendent of Corps DSC Onoja Babayo Samuel, who was arrested by the Federal Capital Territory FCT Police Command for allegedly firing shots into the air during a confrontation with traders at Kubwa Market, Abuja. The Commandant General of the NSCDC, Prof Ahmed Abubakar Audi, also directed that the officer faces an Orderly Room Trial to determine his level of culpability in the alleged offence.",
   "summary_zh": "尼日利亚安全与民防部队（NSCDC）已停职副部队长 DSC 奥诺贾·巴巴约·塞缪尔。联邦首都 Territory FCT 警察司令部以涉嫌在阿布贾库布瓦市场与商贩发生冲突时向空中开枪为由将其逮捕。NSCDC 总司令艾哈迈德·阿布巴卡尔·奥迪教授还指示对该官员进行军纪审判，以确定其在涉嫌犯罪中的责任程度。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Nigeria Security and Civil Defence Corps (NSCDC) has suspended Deputy Superintendent of Corps DSC Onoja Babayo Samuel, who was arrested by the Federal Capital Territory FCT Police Command for allegedly firing shots into the air during a confrontation with traders at Kubwa Market, Abuja. The Commandant General of the NSCDC, Prof Ahmed Abubakar Audi, also directed that the officer faces an Orderly Room Trial to determine his level of culpability in the alleged offence. The National Public Relations Officer of the NSCDC, Assistant Commandant of Corps Babawale Afolabi, disclosed this in a statement issued at the weekend in Abuja. According to the statement, the incident occurred on October 25, and the Corps management has “frowned at the unprofessional conduct of the alleged officer”. Vanguard gathered that the officer’s female acquaintance had been involved in an altercation with a butcher and that an attempt to defend his friend quickly escalated as some unidentified young men had allegedly tried to manhandle him. In the process, eyewitnesses said the officer shot in the air in an apparent bid to scare off those who had descended on him. Afolabi said Audi, “who maintains zero tolerance for misuse of firearms or any form of professional misconduct,” ordered the immediate suspension of the personnel. The proceedings will be handled by what the statement described as “the already well-established committee at the Corps National Headquarters, Abuja”. “The Commandant General reassures members of the public that the NSCDC remains deeply committed to protecting lives and upholding professional standards at all times, no matter the circumstances,” the statement said. Comments expressed here do not reflect the opinions of Vanguard newspapers or any employee thereof",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "sec"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
