   "_dt": 1793445630.0,
   "ageDays": 0.27,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Chief Justice of India Surya Kant will inaugurate the platinum jubilee celebrations of the High Court of Kerala on Sunday (November 1). The ceremony will be held on the High Court premises at 11 a.m. Supreme Court justice Sarasa Venkatanarayana Bhatti and Union Minister of State (Independent Charge) for the Ministry of Law and Justice Arjun Ram Meghwal will be the guests of honour.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后即可解锁。印度首席大法官苏里雅·坎特将于11月1日星期日主持喀拉拉邦高等法院成立75周年庆典。仪式将于上午11时在高等法院院内举行。最高法院法官萨拉萨·文卡塔纳拉亚那·巴蒂以及联邦法律与司法部独立负责的国务部长阿朱恩·拉姆·梅格瓦尔将担任贵宾。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Chief Justice of India Surya Kant will inaugurate the platinum jubilee celebrations of the High Court of Kerala on Sunday (November 1). The ceremony will be held on the High Court premises at 11 a.m. Supreme Court justice Sarasa Venkatanarayana Bhatti and Union Minister of State (Independent Charge) for the Ministry of Law and Justice Arjun Ram Meghwal will be the guests of honour. The inaugural function will be presided over by Chief Justice of the High Court of Kerala Soumen Sen. The inaugural function will also be attended by the chief justices and judges of other High Courts, judges of the High Court of Kerala, former Judges of the Supreme Court of India and the High Courts, among others. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
