   "snippet": "Residents of Waiwayi village in Koko Local Government Area of Kebbi State were seen running for their lives as suspected Lakurawa militants launched a deadly broad daylight attack on civilians. The militants raided Waiwayi, Karwa and Kestu villages around October 26 and 28, burning homes, looting shops and forcing residents to flee toward Koko town. Police confirmed 12 deaths across the attacks, including a police inspector, after joint security teams repelled the assailants.\n\nVideos and local accounts, however, claim up to 20 people were killed in Waiwayi alone, with widespread destruction. The attacks highlight the continuing threat from the group, which is active in Kebbi and Sokoto and carries out raids and cattle rustling, leaving communities gripped by fear.\n\n#CBINewsTV #Lakurawa #Kebbi #Security #Nigeria",
