   "title": "🚨NEW from @GordianKnotRay on WPS Dispatch Sea of Pacification: 🇨🇳#China’s political war for the West Philippine Sea 🇵🇭 Ambassador Jing Quan",
   "url": "https://x.com/SeaLightFound/status/2116192729021731186",
   "snippet": "🚨NEW from @GordianKnotRay on WPS Dispatch \nSea of Pacification: 🇨🇳#China’s political war for the West Philippine Sea 🇵🇭\n\nAmbassador Jing Quan: China \"may easily win\" if it chose force. \"But no, we will not choose force and we love peace,\" so Filipinos should \"feel fortunate that you have a neighbor like China.\"\n\nColonial 🇪🇸Spain had a word for this kind of \"peace\". In 1573, Philip II ordered that conquests be called \"pacifications\". Even 🇺🇸America had ran its own pacification campaign when it replaced Spain as the #Philippines' colonial government in 1898. \n\nIn a new piece for WPS Dispatch, Ray looks at how Beijing is now running its own pacification play in Manila focused on consolidating its control over the West Philippine Sea.\n\nUnderstanding Beijing's rhetoric and how it seeks to reward sympathizers, discredit critics and bring Filipinos to accept the new imperial order is key to building a long-term resistance to China's attempted conquest of the West Philippine Sea. 👇",
   "body": "🚨NEW from @GordianKnotRay on WPS Dispatch \nSea of Pacification: 🇨🇳#China’s political war for the West Philippine Sea 🇵🇭\n\nAmbassador Jing Quan: China \"may easily win\" if it chose force. \"But no, we will not choose force and we love peace,\" so Filipinos should \"feel fortunate that you have a neighbor like China.\"\n\nColonial 🇪🇸Spain had a word for this kind of \"peace\". In 1573, Philip II ordered that conquests be called \"pacifications\". Even 🇺🇸America had ran its own pacification campaign when it replaced Spain as the #Philippines' colonial government in 1898. \n\nIn a new piece for WPS Dispatch, Ray looks at how Beijing is now running its own pacification play in Manila focused on consolidating its control over the West Philippine Sea.\n\nUnderstanding Beijing's rhetoric and how it seeks to reward sympathizers, discredit critics and bring Filipinos to accept the new imperial order is key to building a long-term resistance to China's attempted conquest of the West Philippine Sea. 👇",
